<title>USA: 1997 U.S. FOMC meeting, Beige Book calendar.</title>
<headline>1997 U.S. FOMC meeting, Beige Book calendar.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve has announced its 1997 Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) meeting and Beige Book schedules on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The 1997 FOMC and Beige book meetings will be held on the</p>
<p>following dates:</p>
<p>FOMC 1997			     Beige Book:</p>
<p>Meeting date:</p>
<p>February 4-5 (T-W)		  January 22</p>
<p>March 25				March 12</p>
<p>May 20				  May 7</p>
<p>July 1-2 (T-W)			June 18</p>
<p>August 19			     August 6</p>
<p>September 30			  September 17</p>
<p>November 12 (W)		     October 29</p>
<p>December 16			   December 3</p>
<p>FOMC meetings are held on Tuesdays unless otherwise noted,</p>
<p>the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The FOMC voting members among the Federal Bank presidents</p>
<p>for the next three years are as follows:</p>
<p>January 1, 1997</p>
<p>New York, William McDonough</p>
<p>Richmond, Alfred Broaddus</p>
<p>Atlanta, Jack Guynn</p>
<p>Chicago, Michael Moskow</p>
<p>San Francisco, Rother Parry</p>
<p>January 1, 1998</p>
<p>New York, William McDonough</p>
<p>Boston, Cathy Minehan</p>
<p>Cleveland, Jerry Jordan</p>
<p>St. Louis, Thomas Melzer</p>
<p>Kansas City, Thomas Hoenig</p>
<p>January 1, 1999</p>
<p>New York, William McDonough</p>
<p>Philadelphia, Edward Boehne</p>
<p>Chicago, Michael Moscow</p>
<p>Dallas, Robert McTeer</p>
<p>Minneapolis, Gary Stern</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
